  "question": {
    "text": "What will be the current flowing through the $6 \\mathrm{k} \\Omega$ resistor in the circuit shown, where the breakdown voltage of the Zener is $6 \\mathrm{V} ?$\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2018_phy_q11.png\">",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "CGxoP",
      "text": "$\\frac{2}{3} m A$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Dah9Z",
      "text": "$1 \\mathrm{mA}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "6hcaI",
      "text": "$10 \\mathrm{mA}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "2UjVJ",
      "text": "$\\frac{3}{2} m A$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2018_phy_a11.png\">\r\n\r\nIn the given circuit, the zener diode is used as a voltage regulating device. The voltage across $6 \\mathrm{k} \\Omega$ resistance is $(10-6) \\mathrm{V}=4 \\mathrm{V}$\r\nCurrent through $6 \\mathrm{k} \\Omega$ resistor, $I=\\frac{4 \\mathrm{V}}{6 \\mathrm{k} \\Omega}=\\frac{4}{6 \\times 10^{3}}=\\frac{2}{3} \\times 10^{-3}=\\frac{2}{3} \\mathrm{mA}$",
    "image": null
  },
